{
  "source": "Prompts/Hallucination.mp4",
  "duration": 201.3634375,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.24,
      "text": "Getting ready for a chemistry exam, you ask an AI a simple question."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.96,
      "end": 8.7,
      "text": "Will my Spotify hype playlist help me focus or just distract me?"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.26,
      "end": 13.42,
      "text": "The AI cites a 2022 Stanford study of 1,200 students."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.96,
      "end": 19.36,
      "text": "It claims music improves recall by 18%, recommending volume below 60 decibels."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.9,
      "end": 21.12,
      "text": "This makes it easy to trust."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.58,
      "end": 25.5,
      "text": "But the researchers, the data, the test, the study does not exist."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.02,
      "end": 28.02,
      "text": "This makes the deception difficult to catch."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.02,
      "end": 30.86,
      "text": "The AI isn't generating random gibberish."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.32,
      "end": 36.04,
      "text": "It knows how academic research sounds, attaching invented metrics to real institutions,"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.64,
      "end": 39.24,
      "text": "weaving a lie into an otherwise plausible framework."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.8,
      "end": 45.02,
      "text": "This is a hallucination, a factual claim the AI makes up that sounds true but isn't."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.4,
      "end": 50.84,
      "text": "It bypasses our skepticism by weaponizing the confident, measured tone we expect from reliable sources."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.56,
      "end": 55.94,
      "text": "So why does a piece of software with no personal agenda invent a fake Stanford study?"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.28,
      "end": 59.96,
      "text": "To understand that, we have to look at how these systems construct their answers."
    },
    {
      "start": 60.72,
      "end": 65.3,
      "text": "First, the AI learns from internet text, including mistakes and lies."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.94,
      "end": 67.3,
      "text": "It doesn't retrieve facts."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.78,
      "end": 73.12,
      "text": "It builds responses one token at a time, calculating the most probable next word."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.96,
      "end": 76.86,
      "text": "Trained to be helpful, it generates text to fill silence."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.48,
      "end": 78.0,
      "text": "The result?"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.58,
      "end": 82.04,
      "text": "Answers can be mathematically probable, yet entirely wrong."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.54,
      "end": 85.58,
      "text": "These fabrications are a core feature of the architecture."
    },
    {
      "start": 86.26,
      "end": 94.32,
      "text": "The AI is doing exactly what it was built to do, prioritizing a statistically likely sequence of words over verifying objective truth."
    },
    {
      "start": 95.06,
      "end": 99.72,
      "text": "People often use the term hallucination to describe any mistake an AI makes."
    },
    {
      "start": 100.34,
      "end": 104.82,
      "text": "But there is a distinctly different kind of failure that happens when real data is involved."
    },
    {
      "start": 105.54,
      "end": 110.18,
      "text": "Consider the recent example where users asked an AI how to keep cheese on their pizza."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.18,
      "end": 116.24,
      "text": "The AI confidently instructive users to mix 1 eighth cup of non-toxic glue into the sauce."
    },
    {
      "start": 116.94,
      "end": 121.04,
      "text": "Unlike the fake Stanford study, the AI didn't invent this out of nowhere."
    },
    {
      "start": 121.6,
      "end": 127.6,
      "text": "That bizarre advice traced back to a real source, an old sarcastic joke posted on Reddit."
    },
    {
      "start": 128.36,
      "end": 133.6,
      "text": "The AI successfully scraped the real text, but it completely missed the human context."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.14,
      "end": 138.6,
      "text": "It couldn't detect the sarcasm, so it processed a joke as sincere advice."
    },
    {
      "start": 139.21,
      "end": 141.66,
      "text": "A hallucination invents data from scratch."
    },
    {
      "start": 142.16,
      "end": 145.24,
      "text": "A misinterpretation applies the wrong meaning to real text."
    },
    {
      "start": 145.98,
      "end": 153.46,
      "text": "If an AI can invent a perfectly formatted academic study out of thin air and process obvious jokes into dangerous instructions,"
    },
    {
      "start": 153.78,
      "end": 157.22,
      "text": "it forces us to figure out how to safely use these tools at all."
    },
    {
      "start": 157.86,
      "end": 163.58,
      "text": "You can use these tools effectively without checking every single syllable, provided you know where the guardrails are."
    },
    {
      "start": 163.58,
      "end": 168.1,
      "text": "The most effective digital literacy skill you can develop is an intuition trigger."
    },
    {
      "start": 168.72,
      "end": 172.98,
      "text": "It's paying attention to the subtle feeling when a highly structured claim doesn't add up,"
    },
    {
      "start": 173.2,
      "end": 177.1,
      "text": "or feels a little too perfectly aligned with the exact question you asked."
    },
    {
      "start": 177.8,
      "end": 183.14,
      "text": "Safely navigating an AI-driven world requires accepting its inherent unreliability."
    },
    {
      "start": 183.88,
      "end": 187.1,
      "text": "We have to transition from being passive consumers of information"
    },
    {
      "start": 187.1,
      "end": 190.44,
      "text": "to active investigators of the answers we receive."
    },
    {
      "start": 191.36,
      "end": 194.08,
      "text": "Hallucinations sound like every other AI answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 194.8,
      "end": 197.72,
      "text": "When something doesn't add up, trace the claim to its source."
    }
  ],
